<title>MEXICO: Mexican union movement buys beans, rice - report.</title>
<headline>Mexican union movement buys beans, rice - report.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's umbrella union movement, Confederation of Mexican Workers, bought 400,000 tonnes of dry beans and rice, according to radio.</p>
<p>Network Radio Red said the movement, which groups the vast majority of unions in Mexico and is known as the CTM from its Spanish initials, bought the basic foods and plans to sell them at cut-price levels to union members via mobile shops.</p>
<p>No breakdown was given of quantities. The beans and rice will be put on sale from Jan 8 at prices as much as 50 percent cheaper than market rates, Radio Red said. The beans were bought from producers in Zacatecas state, it added.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
